.TH HTTP_CLOSE 3
.SH NAME
http_close \- close the connection of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_close(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_close ()
shuts down the TLS session if there is one, closes the socket, removes it from the
event loop of io(3) and sets the descriptors in the structure to -1. The buffers, requests
and responses stay as they are, so the response can still be looked at; use
.BR http_free (3)
to release them.
.SH NOTES
When a TLS shutdown has to wait for the socket the wanted direction is registered with io(3) and the socket stays open.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_free(3), tls_close(3)
